==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|B.C.|b.c.|bc}}

===Etymology 1===
{{cal|en|la|ante Christum}}, popularized with the 1627 publication of ''De doctrina temporum'' by French theologian Denis Pétau.

====Adverb====
{{wikipedia|Before Christ}}
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{initialism of|en|[[before|Before]] [[Christ]]}}.
#: {{ux|en|The Han Dynasty ruled China from 206 '''<small>BC</small>''' to <small>AD</small> 220.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1739
|origyear=1735
|author=[[w:Jean-Baptiste Du Halde|P. Du Halde]]
|chapter=Geographical Obſervations on the Kingdom of ''Corea''
|title=The General History Of China
|url=https://archive.org/details/dli.pahar.0011/
|volume=IV
|edition=2nd
|OCLC=51344000
|page=388
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/dli.pahar.0011/page/388/
|text=[...]''Hi vang'', King of ''Yen'' and of ''Corea'', was defeated, taken and killed in the Year 259 '''before the Birth of Chriſt''', according to the Chineſe Hiſtory, and ''Tſin vang'' was acknowledged for Emperor of all ''China'' by the Name of ''Tſin chi hoang ti''.
|brackets=on}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The [[w:Chicago Manual of Style|Chicago Manual of Style]] as well as most house styles require placing the '''AD''' before the number of the year and '''BC''' after, although in casual use either abbreviation can be found in either place.
* Some use [[BCE]], for "Before the Common/Current/Christian Era", which is more secular in nature, to avoid potential Christian bias.
* Often written in [[small caps]].

